      "id": 1,
      "text": "Warren City was founded and incorporated in 1952, carving its own identity in northwestern Gregg and southeastern Upshur counties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/warren-city-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors the Warren Petroleum Corporation, the company that fuels the local economy with natural gas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/warren-city-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Warren City sits inside the East Texas Oil Field, a region that has powered the state’s energy boom for decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warren_City%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Its northern city limits spill into Upshur County, while the western edge borders the town of Gladewater.",
